	"_m320_shotgun": "The M320 and the breaching shotgun (Captain's list for cghath, 2026-10-20), proposed from the catalogue plan (docs/ChrisPlan_handoff.md: weapons 600-4500, explosives 40-600, loose rounds 1-3): M320 1600, 40 mm HE 45 and smoke 35 a grenade, the Skeleton Key (the breaching shotgun, now an underbarrel) 1100, 12 ga shells 2 (standard buck) and 3 (hi-brass, breaching) each. The 870's full choke 250 (one 12-gauge system, 2026-10-21), like a muzzle attachment.",
	"_demolitions": "Demolitions (Captain's list 2026-10-20, Weapons and items), Proposed from the catalogue plan's explosives band (40-600; demo block 500, thermite 250): det cord 60, clacker 150, radio remote 600, claymore 450, AP mine 200, chem lights 40 (IR 60). All in the base shop.",
	"_launchers": "Wave 5 (V2) launchers and rounds, proposed: AT4 1800, NLAW 4000, rounds 200-600, Javelin missile 12000 (catalogue plan); the RPG-7 and its rounds are loot, sell-only. The Javelin is buyable until wave 6 gates it behind reputation.",
	"_heavy_exo": "The HX-1 Assault Frame and its WG-50 (Captain's call, docs/near_future_hardware.md 2.3a, resolved 2026-10-17): priced for repair/salvage valuation (roughly 3x the LX-3 frame's cost, for the bigger chassis and its own weapon mount) but not_for_sale either way — it's issued, not bought, and certified onto a roster soldier (see roles.json / roster.gd hx1_certified) rather than equipped freely.",
	"_allied_only": "Wave 6 (call #1, Captain 2026-10-18: Allied buys \"their best kit, armour\"): not in the base shop; an allied quartermaster (factions.json \"quartermaster\") sells them at Allied standing.",
	"allied_only": ["plate_carrier_heavy", "helmet_heavy", "jammer"],
